 `app_stack_region`, checks its configured stack capacity, populates/writes pages,
 and maps an anonymous heap. The returned tuple is entry address and user SP.
 
+The AArch64 layout reserves an 8-MiB main stack. Only argument pages are
+populated at exec; other stack pages use ordinary anonymous demand faults.
+The fixed reservation also supplies the initial soft/hard `RLIMIT_STACK`
+values through the process runtime. This replaces the 512-KiB AArch64
+capacity that faults on larger desktop application frames. It does not add
+grow-down VMAs or make later rlimit changes resize an existing stack.
+
